3:Every figure in this file is inserted by `tools/generate_trust.py` from the shipped certificates when the package is assembled ({{generated_on}}); none is typed. `tools/shipping_artifact_gate.py` refuses a package in which this file and the certificates disagree.
5:**The one command.** `bash release/build_submission_from_package.sh` rebuilds the submission PDF from the extracted archive and nothing else, and prints `EXTERNAL_PATHS`, `HOME_DEPENDENCIES`, `SESSION_PINNED_INPUTS`, `BUILD_EXIT`, `NEWLY_BUILT_PDF_SHA256` and `SOURCE_MANIFEST_SHA256`. The build's inputs live at `certificates/*_current.log` inside the archive, put there beforehand by `release/stage_build_inputs.sh`, which is a separate step and not part of the build. The build runs in a scratch directory and promotes its outputs only when every preflight and gate has passed; a build that stops at preflight leaves the extracted tree byte-identical (`TREE_UNCHANGED=1`).
