== F9 SEAL_WHAT_IS_OPEN full + provenance
     1	  This round adds the normal-form results of Appendix A to the Lean library. Every SE2-definable total
     2	  function has a full vector coset normal form under one analytic input, TCER (the eventual representation of
     3	  large integers by an individual positive definite ternary lattice coset); without it the full form is proved
     4	  except in the semidefinite branch of polar rank at least three (`generalFullNF_iff_semidefiniteFullNF`,
     5	  `sealedFullNF_of_TCER`). With at least two outputs the conclusion sharpens under TCER to a characterization
     6	  by one integer slope, f(a + Mt) = f(a) + Bt (`singleQuadratic_iff_commonSlope_of_TCER`), whose reverse
     7	  direction holds for every number of outputs without TCER (`singleQuadratic_of_commonSlope`); consequently
     8	  a -> (a^2, 0) is not SE2-definable under TCER although a -> a^2 is (`sqPadFn_not_singleQuadratic_of_TCER`).
     9	  TCER is an explicit hypothesis of the Lean theorems, not an axiom, and the standard-axiom footprint of a
    10	  conditional theorem does not certify it. In ordinary mathematics TCER is the consequence stated on p. 5 of
    11	  the published version of Kane-Kim, specialized to the convention used here in Lemma A.8; formalizing it, or
    12	  replacing it in this application by an argument that avoids the analytic theory, is a separate task. The
    13	  figures of this round -- roots, footprints, frozen statements, pages -- are the measured fields above, and
    14	  this paragraph repeats none of them. The clean-room attestation of this round is one environment (agora);
    15	  see fresh_build_compare above.
    16	  Open: the author sign-off of the rows -- every author field of the regenerated sheet is blank; the final
    17	  locators -- preprint and software DOIs, repository tag, author e-mail -- are unset, so this package is
    18	  built in `draft` mode and the `final` build remains untested on real locators; the blank-slate reviews are
    19	  the reviewer's; the literature items that section 10 records as unresolved remain as section 10 states
    20	  them. The ruling is unchanged and repeated: no Zenodo draft, DOI reservation or GitHub release until every
    21	  content item is fixed and the sheet is signed.
